      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Patients with coronary heart disease and angina pectoris were examined. The blood outflowing from the myocardium at the height of ischemia induced by atrial stimulation was found to have lower levels of fibronectin. Ten minutes after the stimulation discontinuation the concentration of fibronectin returned to baseline. A reduction in the fibronectin content during myocardial ischemia seems to be related to its consumption as a result of maintaining antithrombotic function."},
